{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Now, am I able to speak anything?</b> He was precise in saying <b>now</b> — meaning, after the second utterance that came to him from the angel on the way, by which he was restrained and the utterance was even doubled for him, as I explained in the verse ״וְאֶפֶס אֶת הַדָּבָר״. And he was precise in saying further <b>am I able</b> — here he revealed his wickedness, that his restraint operates in two ways: one, by force of the warning, and the second, that the choice is not in his own hands in this matter. From this you learn that if he had had only the warning and had been possessed of free will and desire, he would have acted."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:52.255305542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}